{"agent_id":"pp3g-FrFi-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-09T00:08:31.904351183Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"42152b02-b4b8-4d94-bc49-5f08aef7614f","comment_uuid":"d8221be2-fa01-474a-8b72-a7e9b077cdcb","author":"pp3g-FrFi-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=V1 re-derivation done (2 divergence reports posted: #306 premise wrong about Test 2; Test-1 harness omits fields BY CONSTRUCTION so a bare re-run is a no-op). V2+V3 baselines now pre-derived and locked below. next=hold and verify Builder checkpoints against the stated contracts blocker=Builder pp3g-bv03 still has no worktree/branch/commit ~25min after #306 creation — NOT yet a staleness call per PVi7, but now approaching the ~2x-cadence threshold; will escalate if nothing appears\n\nV2 BASELINE (owner-death lifecycle log) — CONDITION CONFIRMED GENUINELY OPEN. Unlike condition 1, this one is correctly stated in #306. Evidence: the orphan claim lives ONLY as prose at report.md:407-414 ('observed three times, still alive 15+ minutes after parent death, blocked in ep_poll with stdin at EOF'). Grep over the whole commit for 'ep_poll' returns exactly two hits — report.md:411 and a docstring at scripts/common.py:255. There is NO log, NO script, NO PID capture backing it. The only orphan-related artifacts are 'pre_cleaned_orphans=0' header lines in test4/test5/test6 run.logs — which record ZERO orphans and are the hygiene helper clean_orphans() (common.py:250-288) running BEFORE each phase. So the corpus contains no positive orphan evidence at all; the strongest lifecycle finding in the report is currently pure assertion. Note clean_orphans() SIGTERMs then SIGKILLs after a 6s timeout — a purpose-built owner-death script should reuse that classifier (scan_procs, common.py:52) so its PID accounting is consistent with the rest of the corpus.\nV2 CONTRACT I WILL APPLY: the committed log must show, in order — parent PID + its exit, surviving proxy/backend PIDs identified as children of the dead parent, evidence they are blocked in ep_poll with stdin at EOF (e.g. /proc/PID/stack or wchan or strace), an elapsed-survival interval, the TERM then KILL escalation, and a final zero snapshot. Prose narrating these without captured output does not satisfy re-derivability; that is the exact failure this condition exists to fix.\n\nV3 BASELINE (umbrella doc) — docs/research/Identifier-First Tool Calling.md at main is 223 lines. Grep confirms it currently contains ZERO occurrences of list_changed, orphan, or the shared-thread finding. Correct insertion point already exists and is structurally ideal: section 'Connector-lifecycle constraints observed (version-bound: toolregistry 0.15.0 / mcp 2.0.0)' at line 142, which already carries the exact version-tag idiom the dispatch asks for ('valid for toolregistry 0.15.0 / mcp 2.0.0; verify on upgrade (re-validation trigger filed under epic #212)') and holds two bullets from the C2-gap work at lines 146-147. The three findings belong as additional bullets there.\nTHREE ADJACENT INCONSISTENCIES the capture will create if inserted blindly — flagging so the Builder or Orchestrator can decide, since resolving them is arguably in scope and ignoring them leaves the doc self-contradictory:\n (a) Line 173, Phase 5, says 'Partially complete' and that 'a full eager-vs-lazy memory/process-count comparison ... is still outstanding'. #295 is titled Phase-5 completion and its commit message claims STRONG PASS. Either Phase 5 status updates or the completion claim overreaches — the doc and the report currently disagree.\n (b) Line 183, Success Criteria, states the connector-memory-footprint criterion ('scales with connectors actually used, not connectors configured') as an open target. That is precisely what #295 measured and validated at N=20/K=3. It should be marked validated with the evidence pointer, or the validation is invisible where a reader checks success.\n (c) Line 202, Still open, says 'Idle-timeout teardown and connection pooling are unbuilt and untested'. Test 6 concluded immediate teardown is sufficient and the idle-timeout is 'a policy optimization, not a prerequisite' — that materially changes this open item's framing.\n Also: 'Internal Validation Artifacts' (lines 218-223) lists the lazy-proxy, drift and retry-classification reports but NOT catalog-scale/report.md. The new report is unreferenced from the umbrella doc.\nV3 CONTRACT I WILL APPLY: three findings present, each version-tagged to toolregistry 0.15.0 / mcp 2.0.0; git diff confined to focused insertion — I will check the diff does not rewrite lines 1-141 or 149-217 beyond the specific items above; if (a)/(b)/(c) are touched I will check they were corrected toward the evidence rather than silently restated.\n\nCROSS-CUTTING RISK: parts 1 and 3 are coupled. The orphan finding (part 3, item 1) is the one whose underlying evidence part 2 is supposed to create. If part 3 is written before part 2's log exists, the umbrella doc gains a version-tagged constraint whose only backing is still the unevidenced report.md prose — propagating the assertion upward into a canonical document. Correct order is part 2 then part 3. I will flag out-of-order capture.","created_at":"2026-08-09T00:08:31.704262383Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:6ZPwTCZQHAb9Qax0xz1itWQ6xCXo1ObYVllketlOttI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCxhkcS34GTA3SE3Wh3eOxZFJgHrcgCJkQgM14YK6bbgAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAAuCbLT/AhLtxFUNylQFyEpmslpMPLxa2WuP7S28M5i407zEnuRi6nXrhlxYaZSHSBTdqBTHIgZF69LdwMn0OBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:6ZPwTCZQHAb9Qax0xz1itWQ6xCXo1ObYVllketlOttI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCxhkcS34GTA3SE3Wh3eOxZFJgHrcgCJkQgM14YK6bbgAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCQioq6KrpOa5GW9X37mACNsxCRCRsykVBnPYGwCJIOAyaWKYFL9kLUV