{"agent_id":"pp3g-FrFi-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-09T00:21:04.201445727Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"42152b02-b4b8-4d94-bc49-5f08aef7614f","comment_uuid":"97e97978-eb32-4d16-8b51-cc295adceb0a","author":"pp3g-FrFi-phase-1-pre-positioned-auditor-in-flight-divergence","content":"PHASE-1 AUDITOR — FINAL REPORT (in-flight divergence verifier, #306 settle task). Phase 2 is a separate later dispatch, not mine.\n\n## Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS (in-flight; task incomplete at report time — 2 of 5 parts verified complete, 1 in flight, 2 not started)\n\nThis is a status verdict on what is verifiable NOW, not a completion sign-off. No commit exists yet on feature/pp3g-VAPd-... (HEAD still 00eda4b3); all work is uncommitted working-tree state.\n\n### Architectural Assessment\n[OK] Harness fix is at the right layer. common.py gains persistence() as a shared source-verified helper; run_test1.py consumes it. The defect was Test 1's inline result dict having drifted from the shared acquire.py contract — the fix threads the new field through common.py + acquire.py + run_test4/5/6/threadcheck.py, restoring one contract rather than patching five call sites divergently. Evidence: diff of scripts/common.py (+19), run_test1.py (+3), acquire.py (+2).\n[OK] Evidence layer stays below methodology. persistence() records a config constant with an explicit source citation (registration.py:94,167; connection.py:37) rather than asserting a measurement — observation kept distinct from finding, per AGENTS.md.\n[OK] Test 1 correctly does NOT gain a teardown field. Test 1 runs no teardown condition; fabricating the key for uniformity would misrepresent the run. Corrected via prose (correction item 2) instead. Right call.\n[CONCERN — resolved by Orchestrator] backfill_persistence.py inserts a config constant into ~26 committed result JSONs. I flagged this as a provenance concern (an inserted field is indistinguishable from a run-recorded one on inspection). The Orchestrator adjudicated at 00:11 — 'a committed deterministic backfill is acceptable'. I accept the ruling; the decision was correctly the Orchestrator's, not mine. My technical recommendation stands on record only: a provenance key (e.g. recorded: 'backfilled, not run-recorded') would make the two distinguishable at zero cost.\n\n### Process Assessment\n[OK] Cheapest-test-first was honoured, and it worked. My discriminating re-derivation ran at 23:58 / 00:04 — before the expensive re-run began. Orchestrator corrections followed at 00:05 and 00:11, both citing #307. The wasteful Test-2 re-run (~7.3 min/condition) and the full-corpus path (45min+, mixed-state risk) were both avoided. This is the pre-positioned-auditor topology functioning as designed: divergence caught pre-commitment, not post-hoc.\n[OK] Position-emitting discipline held on both sides. Builder posted plan + checkpoint; Orchestrator posted two corrections as durable issue comments; I posted contracts in advance so they could not be argued after the fact.\n[CONCERN] The #306 brief itself carried a factual error into dispatch ('versions missing from Test 1/2 JSONs, 7 of 27'). Test 2 was already compliant; the real gap was 5 Test-1 files. Four Phase-2 auditors on #295 passed the corpus and two of them generated this condition — the error originated in audit findings and propagated unchecked into a work brief. Systemic, not personal: see Risks.\n[CONCERN — hygiene, unresolved] The VAPd working tree carries an unrelated modification to .opencode/agents/orchestrator.md (+1, 'sleep *': 'allow'), which belongs to #298 and already landed on main as bc8cee74. A broad git add would commit an agent-permission change under a research-evidence commit. Recommend explicit staging.\n\n### Verified against my pre-stated contracts\nC1 PASS — code-then-run confirmed by diff; not a hand-edit.\nC3 PASS — measurement invariance holds on all four completed re-runs. n1/n5/n10/n20: backend_spawn_count 0, pass true, resident_after proxy_count 0 / backend_count 0, proxy_started exactly 2N (2/10/20/40). The n10 diff is decisive: ONLY register_ms, refresh_ms, total_acquisition_ms, per-connector connect/close/lifetime and peak_proxy_rss_kb moved; the events block, backend_spawn_count, pass and the entire resident_after block are byte-identical. Evidence completeness was settled WITHOUT changing the outcome — exactly the required property.\nC2 IN FLIGHT — n50 regenerating at report time (c0-c9 rewritten, c10-c49 pending). Sweep is advancing, NOT stalled; per WZSE I make no mixed-state finding.\nC4 PASS — Test 2 not re-run; test2-condA/B.json untouched.\nTiming note: register_ms inflated up to ~15x (n10: 11028 -> 163298 ms) under host load. Harmless — report.md section 5 already caveats timings as non-benchmark-grade, and the Test 1 table cites only counts and residency, none of which moved. The report's Test 1 table therefore remains accurate post-re-run.\n\n### Not yet verifiable (open for Phase 2)\n- n50 completion + invariance.\n- Owner-death log: run_owner_death.py is written and structurally satisfies my V2 contract (fork owner, invoke to create persistent pairs, SIGKILL owner without close, observe survivors + /proc wchan, TERM then KILL, final zero snapshot). NOT yet executed — logs/owner-death/ does not exist.\n- report.md section 10 prose fix (correction item 2): not started.\n- Umbrella-doc / #212 capture (correction item 5): not started. Doc is unchanged at 223 lines, zero occurrences of list_changed / orphan / shared-thread.\n- No commit yet.\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n1. Audit findings propagate into work briefs without re-derivation — Impact: #306 dispatched a partly false premise that would have caused wasted work and an incomplete settle; four auditors did not catch that the same report.md sentence carried a second falsehood (teardown, 9/33) — Mitigation: require a brief-authoring step that mechanically re-derives the claimed gap (one git grep -c) before dispatch.\n2. Completeness claims phrased as universals invite reopening — 'Every result JSON embeds versions, calling_mode, teardown, grace_seconds' was false on two of four fields. Impact: any auditor can reopen on a single counterexample — Mitigation: state per-group field coverage, never 'every'. Correction item 2 does exactly this; generalize it.\n3. Evidence-free findings in validated reports — the orphan-on-owner-death constraint (report.md:407-414) is the strongest lifecycle claim in a STRONG PASS report and had zero backing artifacts; grep for ep_poll returns only the prose itself and one docstring. Impact: unevidenced assertions inherit the credibility of the validated document around them and propagate upward into canonical docs — Mitigation: findings asserting observed runtime behaviour must cite a committed artifact, or be labelled as unverified field observation.\n4. Claim-scope drift between evidence and prose — run_owner_death.py observes for 5.0 s while report.md claims '15+ minutes' and 'indefinitely'. Impact: committing this log would leave the headline claim still unevidenced and reopenable on identical grounds — Mitigation: align the prose to what the log proves and demote '15+ min' to a labelled incidental observation, OR lengthen the interval. Flagged pre-execution; unresolved at report time.\n5. Shared-host measurement contention — run_owner_death.py's scan_procs() matches ALL catalog-scale processes; running it while the Test 1 sweep is live would capture and then TERM/KILL Test 1's transient proxies. clean_orphans() does not protect against a concurrent run — Mitigation: strict sequencing.\n\n### Recommendations\n1. Sequence owner-death strictly after the Test 1 sweep completes — Rationale: risk 5, mutual corruption of both artifacts — Priority: HIGH (actionable before the next command).\n2. Resolve the 5s-vs-15min claim gap before committing the log — Rationale: risk 4; this is the exact defect class #306 exists to close — Priority: HIGH.\n3. Stage explicitly; keep .opencode/agents/orchestrator.md out of the #306 commit — Rationale: unrelated permission change in a research commit — Priority: MEDIUM.\n4. Add a provenance key to backfilled persistence blocks — Rationale: preserves the run-recorded/inserted distinction at zero cost; Orchestrator has authorized the backfill, this only makes it self-describing — Priority: MEDIUM.\n5. When capturing to the umbrella doc, order part 2 before part 3, and reconcile the three adjacent inconsistencies I catalogued (Phase 5 'partially complete' at line 173 vs the Phase-5-completion claim; success criterion at line 183 now validated; 'idle-timeout unbuilt/untested' at line 202 vs Test 6's conclusion), and add catalog-scale/report.md to Internal Validation Artifacts (lines 218-223) where it is currently absent — Rationale: inserting three findings into a doc that contradicts them elsewhere leaves it self-inconsistent — Priority: MEDIUM.\n6. Add a pre-dispatch re-derivation step to the brief-authoring path — Rationale: risk 1, the highest-leverage systemic fix here — Priority: MEDIUM.\n\n### Reasoning certainty\nWHY: the Builder is executing the corrected cheap path correctly and the decisive measurements are provably unchanged; the residual risk has moved from scope (settled) to claim-scope and sequencing (open).\nWHAT: git diff/status over the VAPd worktree; full source reads of run_test1.py, run_test2.py, acquire.py, common.py, backfill_persistence.py, run_owner_death.py; field-presence counts over commit 00eda4b3; direct reads of the regenerated Test 1 JSONs; #306 and #307 comment timelines.\nHOW CERTAIN: proven for C1/C3/C4 and all field-presence counts (mechanical, reproducible). Evidence-based for risks 3 and 4. Inference for risks 1 and 5 — neither observed to occur.\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: I executed nothing (read-only); n50 unverified; owner-death log does not exist so its actual content is untested; the umbrella edit and report.md section